{"name":"Refuge","hex":"#607d84","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"refuge","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of safety, protection or shelter.","A place providing safety, protection or shelter."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To return to a place of shelter.","To shelter; to protect."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refuge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Area of refuge","blocks":[{"text":"An area of refuge or safe room is a place in a building designed to hold occupants during a fire or other emergency when evacuation may not be safe or possible. Occupants can wait there until rescued or relieved by firefighters."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Area_of_refuge"},{"title":"Bunker","blocks":[{"text":"A bunker is a defensive fortification designed to protect people and valued materials from falling bombs, artillery, or other attacks. Bunkers are almost always underground, in contrast to blockhouses which are mostly above ground. They were used extensively in World War I, World War II, and the Cold War for weapons facilities, command and control centers, storage facilities, etc. Bunkers can also be used as protection from tornadoes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Augarten_Flakturm_Wien2008a.jpg/330px-Augarten_Flakturm_Wien2008a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bunker"},{"title":"Refuge (ecology)","blocks":[{"text":"A refuge is a concept in ecology, in which an organism obtains protection from predation by hiding in an area where it is inaccessible or cannot easily be found. Due to population dynamics, when refuges are available, populations of both predators and prey are significantly higher, and significantly more species can be supported in an area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/20140727--IMG_4412_%2816828865239%29.jpg/330px-20140727--IMG_4412_%28168288652